face-image: img/bankrun.jpg

= The Downturn Arrives

The figures from the Federal Statistical Office leave no room for doubt: the German economy has shrunk for two quarters in a row. New US tariffs, weak demand from China and expensive energy have hit the export industries hardest. Car suppliers in Baden-Württemberg and chemical plants along the Rhine are announcing short-time work, and the Bundesagentur expects unemployment to keep rising for months.

As always, it is the workers who carry the cost of a crisis they did not cause.

- @cap: Recessions come and go. We must keep our nerve.
- @do_something: We must act to protect jobs and incomes.

@cap

Perhaps this is just another turn of the business cycle. Short-time work (Kurzarbeit) will cushion the worst of it, and the downturn may pass on its own.

@do_something
on-arrival: crisis_urgency += 1

How to protect jobs and incomes is quickly becoming the most hotly debated question in the party.
